  "finite_family_proof_notes": {
    "hud": "Every true return contains one of nine exact address equalities. Enabled/memory/actor/meter/leaf state only narrows it. The host wrapper only forwards; it does not refresh identity or initialize state.",
    "health": "candidate(address) is mandatory before pending[] comparison. Its six equalities plus the immutable eight-entry damage-return table bound even arbitrary active pending return_pc values. LR/config/owner/outer-active restrictions only narrow. requested/identity are plain read-only predicates; no cancellation/attachment runs here.",
    "quick": "The first rejection limits to frame/ship entry/ship return/execute and seven exact proc_address equalities. Overlay, config, pending, crane/fire can enable only these keys; dynamic g_pending is not an address wildcard. Off-domain returns before bluewake_quick_items_enabled.",
    "dialogue": "Only six literal addresses reach true or pending scans. Pending entries contribute active booleans, never return-address matches. Off-domain never calls multiplier or reads guest memory.",
    "enhancement": "An explicit four-address rejection precedes CPU/config/LR checks. Canonical LR only gates commit/animation at those addresses; active wind/boots enable only fixed returns. No arbitrary LR or pending-return address expands the domain.",
    "autosave": "Only SERIALIZE/POLL/FPU_REOWN/private return/frame can be true. Atomic public_phase/config activity is consulted only at those addresses; off-domain short-circuits false. Atomic changes cannot enlarge this set."
  },
  "static_excluded_main_slots": 5262,
  "maintenance": "Whole-source pins intentionally conservative. Review complete true domains and live policy for changes; updating hashes alone is not recertification. Regenerate the exact table and rerun implication/lifetime/runtime qualification. Unknown profile or source disables only this optional shortcut.",
